<v Ira Glass>Wait, wait. Surgery? You mean like, surgery surgery? Like, they cut into you?
<v Ira Glass>等等，等等。手术？你是说像，那种外科手术？就像，他们会切开你的身体？

00:18:37.930 --> 00:18:55.230
<v Davy Rothbart>Well, no, it's psychic surgery. You're told this is how it works. Basically, you just sit in this room with 20 other people in a chair and the entities perform surgery on you. You just can't see it happen. I mean, Joao is not even in the room.
<v Davy Rothbart>嗯，不，是精神外科手术。你被告知手术就是这么进行的。基本上，你只需要和另外20个人坐在一间房的椅子上，实体就会为你进行手术。你只是看不见它发生。我的意思是，若昂甚至都不在房间里。

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:57.130
<v Ira Glass>And you get the surgery, too?
<v Ira Glass>你也做了手术吗？

00:18:57.130 --> 00:19:03.050
<v Davy Rothbart>Yeah, I get surgery, too. I mean, I sit next to my mom and we have the surgery together.
<v Davy Rothbart>是的，我也做了手术。我的意思是，我和妈妈坐在一起，我们一起做了手术。

00:19:03.050 --> 00:19:37.250
<v Davy Rothbart>I'm sitting here and my mom is next to me and she's breathing. I can feel her breathing really slowly and sort of intensely. And I'm not feeling anything, but I don't know. I'm hoping she's experiencing something. It seems strange now, but I was so kind of disoriented. And just everything was so weird. I never really felt like I had steady footing. I didn't know what was going on. I don't know, I felt like maybe it could all be real.
<v Davy Rothbart>我坐在那里，妈妈就在我旁边，她在呼吸。我能感觉到她呼吸得非常缓慢且专注。我没感觉到什么，但我不清楚。我希望她能体验到什么。现在回想起来觉得很奇怪，但我当时太困惑了。一切都太诡异了。我从未觉得自己的脚步是稳的。我不知道发生了什么。不知道，我感觉也许这一切可能是真的。

00:19:37.250 --> 00:20:09.210
<v Davy Rothbart>Heather, she warns us. She says, you know, don't be too active right after invisible surgery, because you can rip out the invisible sutures that the entities have just put in. She says, you've got to treat it just like you would conventional surgery. And just stay in bed. And in fact, after these invisible surgeries, we were both totally exhausted. And we went to our rooms and we just slept soundly, totally for about 24 hours.
<v Davy Rothbart>希瑟警告我们。她说，你知道，隐形手术后不要太活跃，因为你可能会撕裂实体刚刚缝合好的隐形缝线。她说，你必须像对待常规手术一样对待它。待在床上。事实上，在这些隐形手术后，我们两个都精疲力竭了。我们回到了房间，睡得很沉，一共睡了大约24小时。

00:20:09.210 --> 00:20:30.450
<v Davy Rothbart>The next morning, I wake up and I can look down and see there's been no miracle for my skin. I'm not cured. And it was really humid, so my tape recorder was sticking a little bit. So the sound's a little bit funny, but this is tape of me just kind of going down to visit my mom for the first time after the surgery.
<v Davy Rothbart>第二天早上，我醒来往下看，发现我的皮肤并没有奇迹发生。我没有被治愈。当时湿度很大，所以我录音机的带子有点粘住。所以声音有点奇怪，但这录音是我手术后第一次去看我妈妈。

00:20:30.450 --> 00:20:50.440
<v Davy Rothbart>It's the morning after surgery and I feel pretty groggy. I slept almost 24 hours straight, and I'm ravenous. I'm going to go down to breakfast and see if my mom can hear again.
<v Davy Rothbart>这是手术后的早晨，我觉得有点昏昏沉沉。我连续睡了快24小时，饿极了。我要去吃早餐，看看我妈能不能听见了。

00:20:50.440 --> 00:21:05.220
<v Davy Rothbart>Going downstairs. I hear some voices down there on breakfast. There she is. She's talking to someone. Well, she's looking at something.
<v Davy Rothbart>下楼了。我在早餐时听到了一些声音。她在那儿。她在和某人说话。嗯，她在看某样东西。

00:21:05.220 --> 00:21:14.330
<v Davy Rothbart>Hey Mom. Mom. I'm right behind you. She doesn't see me.
<v Davy Rothbart>嘿，妈妈。妈妈。我就在你后面。她没看见我。

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:31.640
<v Davy Rothbart>Hey Mom. Mom. I'm right in your ear. Mom, can you hear me? Can you hear me? She can't hear me.
<v Davy Rothbart>嘿，妈妈。妈妈。我就在你耳边。妈妈，你能听见吗？你能听见吗？她听不见我。

00:21:31.640 --> 00:21:45.660
<v Ira Glass>OK, so clearly at this point, you probably realize like, OK, your mom didn't get her hearing back. Did they warn you that it wasn't going to be like, OK, man puts his hands on you and, kaboom, you know, that suddenly you get your hearing back? But that it might take weeks or more?
<v Ira Glass>好了，显然到了这一点，你可能意识到，好吧，你妈妈没有恢复听力。他们有没有警告过你，这不是那种“某人手放在你身上，砰的一声，你突然就能听见了”的那种？而是可能需要几周甚至更久？

00:21:45.660 --> 00:22:12.720
<v Davy Rothbart>Yeah. They said there's a whole range of possibilities. Some people are healed instantly. Some people, it takes a couple of weeks. Some people, a couple months. Some people, a couple years. But still, change will happen a little bit at a time. So I tapped her on the shoulder and I asked her if she felt any different? And she said she thought she felt like a greater sensitivity to vibration. Maybe it could be a sign that her hearing was coming back. And then she asked me how I was feeling.
<v Davy Rothbart>是的。他们说可能性有很多种。有些人立即痊愈。有些人需要几周。有些人几个月。有些人几年。但无论如何，变化会一点一点发生。所以我拍了拍她的肩膀，问她感觉有什么不同吗？她说她觉得对振动的敏感度提高了。也许这可能是她听力正在恢复的迹象。然后她问我感觉怎么样。

00:22:12.720 --> 00:22:14.610
<v Barbara>How are you feeling?
<v Barbara>你感觉怎么样？

00:22:14.610 --> 00:22:32.740
<v Davy Rothbart>I don't feel so great. It's either the invisible surgeries and the sutures within me, or it's the runs.
<v Davy Rothbart>我感觉不太好。要么是因为隐形手术和体内的缝线，要么是因为腹泻。

