<v Ken>I don't tell jokes. I only channel jokes from the entities.
<v Ken>我不讲笑话。我只传导来自实体的笑话。

00:23:10.860 --> 00:23:26.140
<v Davy Rothbart>This is a few days after our surgeries, and there's sort of a town talent show. I'm translating all of this into sign language for my mom. Most of us foreigners are here for several weeks, so the town's got this whole kind of summer camp feeling.
<v Davy Rothbart>这是我们手术后几天了，镇上举行了一个才艺秀。我把这一切都翻译成手语给我妈看。我们大多数外国人都在这里待上几周，所以镇上有一种夏令营的感觉。

00:23:26.140 --> 00:23:36.480
<v Davy Rothbart>This is Ken and his doctors at home had given him a few weeks to live. He's got some kind of severe liver problem and he's supposed to die soon.
<v Davy Rothbart>这是肯，他家乡的医生让他只剩几周的生命了。他患有某种严重的肝病，很快就会去世。

00:23:36.480 --> 00:23:39.600
<v Ken>How many entities does it take to change a light bulb?
<v Ken>换个灯泡需要几个实体？

00:23:39.600 --> 00:23:41.210
<v Announcer>How many?
<v Announcer>几个？

00:23:41.210 --> 00:23:47.500
<v Ken>Zero, we've already seen the light.
<v Ken>零个，我们已经看见光明了。

00:23:47.500 --> 00:24:12.210
<v Davy Rothbart>So you basically do the same thing every day. Take the pills, you either see Joao, or you spend more time in that current room, the meditation room. And people are so nice. A lot of them are really down to earth. They're really cool and just really friendly. And so I am getting along with people and it's sort of powerful just to be around so many people that have cancer, AIDS, people that are really close to dying.
<v Davy Rothbart>所以基本上你每天做同样的事情。吃药，要么去看若昂，要么在那间电流房、冥想室里待更久。人们都特别好。很多都很脚踏实地。他们真的很酷，而且特别友好。所以我跟大家相处得不错，身处这么多癌症、艾滋病、临近死亡的人身边，这种感觉挺震撼的。

00:24:12.210 --> 00:24:14.600
<v Ken>Why didn't the entity cross the road?
<v Ken>为什么实体没过马路？

00:24:14.600 --> 00:24:17.630
<v Announcer>Why?
<v Announcer>为什么？

00:24:17.630 --> 00:24:19.990
<v Ken>He was already on the other side.
<v Ken>他已经在对面了。

00:24:19.990 --> 00:24:23.440
<v Ken>[LAUGHTER AND APPLAUSE]
<v Ken>[笑声和掌声]

00:24:23.440 --> 00:25:09.600
<v Davy Rothbart>The problem is, everyone's telling you these miracle stories all the time, just constant miracle stories, but you don't see any miracles. People in wheelchairs are still in wheelchairs. Blind folks are still blind. They're like urban legends. And it's like they can smell my skepticism. It's like the way animals can smell fear. And to them, everything that happens, everything that goes on there proves that they're right and that these entities exist. You know, like my back was just starting to kill because you're sitting in this current room for just hours and hours on end. They told me that the pain was proof that the entities are working on me. And I was like--
<v Davy Rothbart>问题是，每个人都在不断地告诉你这些奇迹故事，没完没了的奇迹故事，但你却一个奇迹都没看见。坐轮椅的人依然坐轮椅。盲人依然失明。它们就像都市传说。而且感觉他们能闻到我的怀疑。就像动物能闻到恐惧一样。对他们来说，发生的每一件事，在那里发生的每一件事，都证明了他们是对的，证明了这些实体存在。你知道，比如我的背部开始剧痛，因为你在那电流室里一坐就是好几个小时。他们告诉我疼痛证明了实体正在为我治疗。而我就像……

00:25:09.600 --> 00:25:15.330
<v Ira Glass>So in their view, is there like even room for coincidence? Or--?
<v Ira Glass>所以在他们看来，甚至有巧合的余地吗？还是……？

00:25:15.330 --> 00:25:33.810
<v Davy Rothbart>No. No, anything that happens, whatever happens, happens for a reason. And I mean, it would be one thing if they just asked me to believe or just to try to believe, but they all tried to convince me that it's based on science. Here's a couple examples.
<v Davy Rothbart>没有。不，发生的任何事情，无论发生什么，都是有原因的。我的意思是，如果他们只是让我去相信或只是尝试去相信那还好，但他们都试图说服我这是基于科学。这儿有几个例子。

00:25:33.810 --> 00:25:39.850
<v Woman 1>Our hearts create a field of energy around our bodies. We know this now. We can measure it.
<v Woman 1>我们的心脏在我们的身体周围产生一个能量场。我们现在知道了。我们可以测量它。

00:25:39.850 --> 00:25:47.070
<v Man 1>Each of us holds a vibration, and that vibration attracts other like vibrations and affects other vibrations.
<v Man 1>我们每个人都带着一种振动，这种振动吸引其他类似的振动并影响其他振动。

00:25:47.070 --> 00:25:58.220
<v Woman 1>We also know that medium Joao has been hooked up to electrodes and that he goes down to 0 resistance. So he becomes like a lightning rod.
<v Woman 1>我们还知道通灵者若昂曾连接过电极，他的电阻降到了0。所以他变得像一根避雷针。

00:25:58.220 --> 00:26:05.640
<v Woman 2>Because I'm a Capricorn, I have bad knees. And I felt them working on my knees, and I also felt them working on my elbow.
<v Woman 2>因为我是摩羯座，我的膝盖不好。我感觉到他们在治疗我的膝盖，我也感觉到他们在治疗我的手肘。

00:26:05.640 --> 00:26:08.000
<v Davy Rothbart>Capricorns are known for having bad knees?
<v Davy Rothbart>摩羯座以膝盖不好闻名？

00:26:08.000 --> 00:26:12.220
<v Woman 2>Yeah.
<v Woman 2>是的。

00:26:12.220 --> 00:26:32.320
<v Davy Rothbart>For my mom, the longer her hearing is not coming back, the more obsessed she kind of becomes with just following every little rule of the place. Like, Heather told us we have to stock up on holy water, the holy water they have at the Casa gift shop. And it's really just a regular brand of-- it's just bottled water, but it's been blessed by the entities.
<v Davy Rothbart>对我妈来说，她的听力迟迟没有恢复，她就变得越发沉迷于遵守这个地方的所有小规则。比如，希瑟告诉我们必须囤积圣水，Casa礼品店里的圣水。其实它就是一个普通的品牌——就是瓶装水，但经过了实体的祝福。

00:26:32.320 --> 00:26:37.680
<v Davy Rothbart>And here, me and my mom are at breakfast. And my mom catches me drinking the regular bottled water.
<v Davy Rothbart>这儿，我和我妈在吃早餐。我妈发现我正在喝普通的瓶装水。

